    {
      "id": "zf9lfmo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.4 IT Infrastructure for Banks"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "RTGS settles transactions continuously on an individual basis with a minimum threshold of ₹2 Lakhs, whereas NEFT settles in half-hourly net batches with no minimum limit.",
        "NPCI (National Payments Corporation of India) was established in 2008 under the Payment and Settlement Systems Act, 2007.",
        "RBI guidelines require regulated entities to report any major cyber security incident to the RBI within 2 to 6 hours of detection."
      ],
      "id": "a3lj6p2"
    },
